WEBVTT

00:00.599 --> 00:02.399
Kia ora, and welcome to Protecting

00:02.399 --> 00:04.120
Vulnerable Road Users in Temporary

00:04.120 --> 00:05.960
Traffic Management, a Sela Civil

00:05.960 --> 00:07.640
course. This course is about the

00:07.640 --> 00:09.000
people on and around your site

00:09.000 --> 00:10.027
who aren't in a vehicle.

00:11.507 --> 00:15.027
What a nice day for a walk.

00:16.306 --> 00:19.987
Catching the bus is so easy.

00:20.174 --> 00:21.694
Vulnerable road users are people

00:21.694 --> 00:23.374
walking, people on bikes and

00:23.374 --> 00:24.694
scooters, and people catching the

00:24.694 --> 00:26.214
bus. They are the most likely to

00:26.214 --> 00:28.094
be badly hurt, and historically

00:28.094 --> 00:29.254
they've been the last people we

00:29.254 --> 00:30.081
plan for.

00:30.121 --> 00:31.841
Over six modules we'll cover who

00:31.841 --> 00:33.720
these people are, how to plan for

00:33.720 --> 00:35.920
people on foot and on wheels, bus

00:35.920 --> 00:38.121
stops, level crossings, and how to

00:38.121 --> 00:40.108
check your site once it's set up.

00:40.748 --> 00:42.507
Next unlocks when each slide

00:42.507 --> 00:43.787
finishes

00:43.787 --> 00:45.867
and each module ends with a short

00:45.867 --> 00:47.947
knowledge check.

00:47.947 --> 00:50.135
Let's get started.
